WEBVTT

00:02.183 --> 00:04.953
♪ it seems today
that all you see ♪

00:05.021 --> 00:08.295
♪ is violence in movies
and sex on tv ♪

00:08.363 --> 00:11.902
♪ but where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.969 --> 00:14.607
♪ on which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.675 --> 00:18.180
♪ lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:18.248 --> 00:21.621
♪ lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.689 --> 00:23.225
♪ all the things that make us ♪

00:23.293 --> 00:25.029
♪ laugh and cry ♪

00:25.096 --> 00:28.268
♪ he's... A...
Fam... Ily... Guy! ♪

00:35.216 --> 00:37.821
How's the garage sale
going, quagmire?
Pretty good.

00:37.889 --> 00:39.825
Just clearing some of my stuff
out of the basement.

00:39.892 --> 00:42.330
It's amazing what you find
when you clean your basement.

00:42.397 --> 00:44.568
Peter, you almost done
down there?

00:44.636 --> 00:46.171
(laughing)

00:46.238 --> 00:47.708
Look what I found.

00:47.775 --> 00:49.444
That's wonderful, peter.

00:49.511 --> 00:52.049
Now, if you'll excuse me,
I'm gonna go do some skywriting.

00:58.263 --> 01:00.834
(cackling)

01:00.901 --> 01:04.742
Hey, look at all these videos
mr. Quagmire's selling.

01:04.809 --> 01:07.914
<i>Wow, the best of the world's
wildest police chases.</i>

01:07.982 --> 01:10.487
(gasps)
and it even has the one
with the flintstones!

01:11.490 --> 01:13.091
(horns honking)

01:13.160 --> 01:15.196
<i>Announcer:
Amazingly, this drunk driver</i>

01:15.264 --> 01:17.501
<i>Turns left
into oncoming traffic!</i>

01:17.568 --> 01:19.806
<i>He narrowly misses
hitting a pedestrian</i>

01:19.874 --> 01:21.977
<i>Who jumps out of the way
just in time.</i>

01:22.046 --> 01:23.414
<i>Now the driver can add</i>

01:23.481 --> 01:25.685
<i>Attempted battery
to the charges.</i>

01:25.752 --> 01:27.689
<i>The driver turns right
into the parking lot</i>

01:27.755 --> 01:29.893
<i>Of a drive-in movie theater.</i>

01:29.960 --> 01:33.734
<i>At this point,
the dinosaur in the back seat</i>

01:33.802 --> 01:35.370
<i>Pokes his head up
through the roof</i>

01:35.439 --> 01:38.243
<i>And the driver places two
small children on top of it.</i>

01:38.311 --> 01:41.383
<i>Now he's not only
endangering his own life,</i>

01:41.451 --> 01:44.522
<i>But their lives as well.</i>

01:44.590 --> 01:47.496
<i>The driver totals the car
and makes a run for it,</i>

01:47.564 --> 01:50.669
<i>But the pursuing officers
are prepared.</i>

01:50.737 --> 01:52.205
<i>Running from the cops?</i>

01:52.272 --> 01:54.442
<i>Yabba-dabba-don't!</i>

01:54.511 --> 01:58.384
Hey, quagmire, I think I might
wanna buy this ham radio off ya.

01:58.452 --> 01:59.754
Sure, peter,
that'll be 50 dollars.

01:59.821 --> 02:01.289
50 bucks?

02:01.357 --> 02:02.893
All right, fine,
I'll buy it.

02:02.961 --> 02:05.297
Man, this is a bigger rip-off
than shrunky dinks.

02:05.366 --> 02:08.004
They already been shrunk.

02:08.072 --> 02:09.640
Happy "birthmas."

02:13.182 --> 02:16.187
(static crackling)

02:16.255 --> 02:18.692
Peter, you been fiddling with
that ham radio for seven weeks.

02:18.760 --> 02:20.095
Take a shower!

02:20.163 --> 02:22.801
I can barely get any reception
on this stupid thing.

02:22.867 --> 02:25.338
So far the only station that
comes in is some british guys

02:25.406 --> 02:27.644
Reading news from places
I'm not sure exist.

02:27.711 --> 02:30.783
Today, in kuzikistan,
a peaceful demonstration

02:30.851 --> 02:33.389
Turned to bloodshed as members
of the turzirly tribe

02:33.456 --> 02:35.626
Flooded kenpao square
in remembrance

02:35.694 --> 02:38.532
Of the third anniversary
of the hormsburg massacre.

02:38.600 --> 02:41.605
But finally, some good news
out of neighboring kanduzi,

02:41.673 --> 02:44.076
As locals there have reached
an uneasy alliance

02:44.145 --> 02:46.415
With the bordering
trolika bubsie wubsie dal.

02:46.482 --> 02:49.521
And now with sports,
here's framptal tromwibbler.

02:49.589 --> 02:52.260
From the world of sport,
the cointen spinky whompers

02:52.327 --> 02:54.397
Flumped the floing boing
welfencloppers,

02:54.465 --> 02:56.702
70-fluff to 40-flabe.

02:56.769 --> 02:58.907
At the tone, the time
will be 26 railroad.

02:58.975 --> 03:00.209
(tone beeps)

03:00.277 --> 03:02.013
I'm not sure about any of that.

03:02.081 --> 03:04.451
<i>You know, dad, I saw
that movie white noise,</i>

03:04.519 --> 03:06.623
And they said you can
use empty radio static

03:06.690 --> 03:08.393
To talk to dead people.

03:08.461 --> 03:10.029
You idiot, ghosts don't exist.

03:10.097 --> 03:12.401
Wait a second. They might.

03:12.469 --> 03:14.604
(static crackling)

03:14.673 --> 03:16.676
Hello, ghosts.

03:16.744 --> 03:18.078
Come in, ghosts.

03:18.146 --> 03:19.282
Man:
Hello?

03:19.349 --> 03:20.651
Hello? Who's this?

03:20.718 --> 03:22.288
This is ronald reagan.

03:22.355 --> 03:23.657
Ronald reagan?

03:23.724 --> 03:25.694
The guy that used to bang
that 70-pound witch?

03:25.762 --> 03:28.734
Ronald reagan, former
president of the United States.

03:28.802 --> 03:30.337
Oh, my god!

03:30.405 --> 03:32.408
(dialing)

03:32.476 --> 03:35.782
Hey, quagmire, guess who
I'm talking to right now?

03:35.849 --> 03:37.017
Yep!

03:40.625 --> 03:42.762
Brian, will you take me
down to baby gap?

03:42.830 --> 03:44.633
I want to dress
like a small douche.

03:44.701 --> 03:45.969
No, maybe tomorrow or Tuesday.

03:46.036 --> 03:47.504
But you said you'd do it today.

03:47.572 --> 03:48.574
Eh, I'm kinda tired.

03:48.642 --> 03:49.876
Oh, for god's sake.

03:49.944 --> 03:51.312
Cancel my Tuesday appointments!

03:51.380 --> 03:52.749
Sure thing, stewie.

03:52.817 --> 03:54.519
You want me to move it
to another day?

03:54.587 --> 03:55.621
No, no, just cancel it.

03:55.689 --> 03:57.994
Okay, will do.

03:58.061 --> 03:59.329
Who the hell was that?
Hmm?

03:59.397 --> 04:00.965
There was another
stewie right there.

04:01.033 --> 04:03.237
Oh, yeah, well, you know,
I've been so damn busy lately,

04:03.305 --> 04:04.706
My schedule's been so packed,

04:04.774 --> 04:06.710
I felt like I needed
some kind of an errand boy

04:06.778 --> 04:08.749
To do all my nitpicky,
pain-in-the-ass stuff.

04:08.816 --> 04:09.983
So I cloned myself.

04:10.052 --> 04:11.687
You... You cloned yourself?

04:11.755 --> 04:13.124
What are you deaf?

04:13.192 --> 04:16.096
So he's an exact
copy of you?
Well, not exact.

04:16.164 --> 04:17.532
I have to remain superior

04:17.600 --> 04:19.169
So I bred out some
of the intelligence.

04:19.237 --> 04:20.873
Made him sort of
a simpleton, you know.

04:20.940 --> 04:22.442
I call him bitch stewie.

04:22.510 --> 04:24.881
Would you like to meet him?

04:24.948 --> 04:27.820
Would you like
to meet bitch stewie?

04:27.889 --> 04:29.123
Uh, yeah, I guess.

04:29.191 --> 04:30.659
Bitch stewie!

04:30.727 --> 04:32.195
Come here and meet
my friend, brian.

04:32.263 --> 04:33.497
Hey, there, stewie.

04:33.566 --> 04:35.202
Oh, what's that?
You got a friend?

04:35.269 --> 04:37.138
Oh, I'm always happy to meet
one of your friends.

04:37.206 --> 04:38.876
Dear god.

04:38.943 --> 04:40.879
How do you do?
Pleased to meet you.
I'm bitch stewie.

04:40.947 --> 04:42.416
He's got quite a grip.

04:42.485 --> 04:45.022
Hey, bitch stewie, why are
there no midget accountants?

04:45.090 --> 04:47.393
Because they always
come up short.

04:47.461 --> 04:49.030
(laughing)

04:49.098 --> 04:50.867
Oh, another good one, stewie!

04:50.935 --> 04:52.336
I don't know where
you come up with them.

04:52.404 --> 04:54.006
Isn't he wonderful?

04:54.074 --> 04:55.477
And all I have to feed him
is a crude peanut paste.

04:55.543 --> 04:56.411
Watch this.

04:58.450 --> 05:00.453
Uh-huh!

05:00.521 --> 05:01.956
It's not much,
but it's healthier

05:02.023 --> 05:03.425
Than what people
ate in the '50s.

05:03.494 --> 05:04.928
Steak and donut
sandwich, please.

05:04.996 --> 05:06.232
You want cigarettes
on that sandwich?

05:06.299 --> 05:07.601
What do I look like?
A mary?

05:07.668 --> 05:08.769
Yes, I want cigarettes!

05:12.144 --> 05:14.046
Okay, next up on the stage,

05:14.114 --> 05:17.320
Let's have a big karaoke welcome
for peter and ron!

05:17.388 --> 05:18.824
(light applause)

05:18.892 --> 05:20.928
Okay, this is one
of our favorites.

05:20.996 --> 05:23.131
Hope it's one of yours.

05:23.200 --> 05:25.971
♪ ♪

05:29.479 --> 05:32.384
♪ don't go breaking my heart ♪

05:32.451 --> 05:33.954
(feedback squealing)
♪ I couldn't... ♪

05:34.023 --> 05:35.824
(screaming)
ow!

05:35.892 --> 05:39.899
♪ oh, honey, if I get restless ♪

05:39.967 --> 05:41.236
♪ baby, you're... ♪
(feedback squealing)

05:41.304 --> 05:43.006
(screaming)

05:45.946 --> 05:49.385
♪ don't go breaking my heart ♪

05:49.453 --> 05:52.225
(feedback squealing)
(screaming)

05:52.292 --> 05:56.901
♪ oh, honey, when I knock
on your door ♪

05:56.969 --> 05:59.607
(feedback squealing)
(screaming)

06:03.815 --> 06:05.618
Oh, sorry, didn't realize
somebody was in here.

06:05.685 --> 06:07.155
What the hell?

06:07.222 --> 06:09.392
Oh, hello, brian.

06:09.460 --> 06:10.895
Oh, there's your
friend, brian!

06:10.963 --> 06:12.232
Hey, brian!

06:12.300 --> 06:14.737
I sure did enjoy talking
to you the other day!

06:14.804 --> 06:17.241
I'm just making sure
stewie is nice and clean

06:17.310 --> 06:19.346
For his trip to the playground
this afternoon.

06:19.414 --> 06:21.217
We had a little bit
of a problem earlier

06:21.285 --> 06:23.755
Because bitch stewie was
stooling in the tub, wasn't he?

06:23.822 --> 06:24.991
I did some poos.

06:25.059 --> 06:26.694
I did some poos
I didn't mean to.

06:26.762 --> 06:28.799
But we've rectified that now,
and everything's fine.

06:28.867 --> 06:30.135
This is really weird.

06:30.202 --> 06:31.637
I mean, it's one thing
to have him help you out

06:31.705 --> 06:33.073
With a busy schedule.

06:33.141 --> 06:34.477
It's another thing
to let him wash your back.

06:34.545 --> 06:36.448
Well, he does more
than that, brian.

06:36.516 --> 06:38.151
Bitch stewie, give
me a bubble beard.

06:39.555 --> 06:42.592
Look at me, I'm
george bernard shaw.

06:42.660 --> 06:44.864
(laughing):
That's awful funny, stewie!

06:44.932 --> 06:47.303
I don't know who
george bernard shaw is,

06:47.371 --> 06:49.673
But you look like
an old stewie, stewie.

06:49.742 --> 06:51.878
Enjoy your weird bath.

06:51.946 --> 06:53.816
I told him I did the poos

06:53.883 --> 06:55.553
Even though you did
the poos, stewie.

06:55.620 --> 06:57.255
Did I do good, stewie?

06:57.323 --> 06:58.959
That was very correct
of you, bitch stewie.

06:59.027 --> 07:00.563
You're a good helper.

07:04.905 --> 07:06.675
Reagan:
And what a lot
of people don't know

07:06.743 --> 07:09.114
Is that I was
jane wyman's first.

07:09.181 --> 07:11.318
You might say
I broke her jane wyman.

07:11.387 --> 07:13.356
(all laughing)

07:13.423 --> 07:14.725
Oh, reagan is a delight!

07:14.793 --> 07:16.428
He sure is, and you
know what else?

07:16.497 --> 07:19.735
The ghost of reagan
is gonna be the new
fourth guy in our group.

07:19.803 --> 07:21.004
I'm all for that.

07:21.072 --> 07:22.408
What other stories
you got, reagan?

07:22.475 --> 07:23.910
Well, I remember the time

07:23.978 --> 07:26.649
I invited ed sullivan
to the white house.

07:26.717 --> 07:28.753
He sounded a little
something like this:

07:28.821 --> 07:31.459
(imitating ed sullivan):
Hey, ron, tonight we got
a really big show.

07:31.527 --> 07:33.496
Ah, reagan
does impressions!

07:33.564 --> 07:34.933
That's right.

07:35.001 --> 07:36.302
And you know who else
does impressions?

07:36.370 --> 07:37.838
Rich little.

07:37.906 --> 07:40.778
In fact, you ought to go see his
show at the mohegan sun casino

07:40.846 --> 07:43.081
Next Saturday
at 3:00 pm and 5:00 pm.

07:43.149 --> 07:44.852
Wait a second.

07:44.920 --> 07:46.556
Yeah, no (bleep).
What?

07:46.623 --> 07:47.826
Peter, that's not ronald reagan.

07:47.893 --> 07:48.994
That's rich little!

07:49.062 --> 07:50.430
You're rich little!

07:50.498 --> 07:52.434
He must be on his
own ham radio!

07:52.502 --> 07:54.338
(imitating johnny carson):
Ah, well, uh, you know, ed,

07:54.406 --> 07:57.278
The kids say you gotta go viral
to promote yourself these days.

07:57.346 --> 07:58.747
So, this is not reagan?

07:58.815 --> 07:59.883
No, it's rich little.

07:59.951 --> 08:01.119
He's an impressionist.

08:01.187 --> 08:02.322
He's been screwing
with your head.

08:02.389 --> 08:03.791
Well, this thing
is worthless!

08:03.859 --> 08:05.728
Like my palestinian
alarm clock.

08:06.931 --> 08:08.901
Allahu akbar!

08:16.618 --> 08:17.586
Hey, peter, what's up?

08:17.654 --> 08:18.889
Hey, quagmire, uh, listen,

08:18.956 --> 08:21.193
I'm here to get my money
back for that ham radio.

08:21.261 --> 08:22.763
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa,
slow down there, partner.

08:22.831 --> 08:24.199
All sales are final.

08:24.267 --> 08:26.336
Yeah, but you were agamemnon
with me during the sale.

08:26.404 --> 08:27.672
What?

08:27.741 --> 08:29.777
I just saw that word somewhere.
I wanted to use it.

08:29.845 --> 08:32.149
Look, peter, why don't you just
go home before you get hurt?

08:32.217 --> 08:33.518
Well, I'm clearly
not the only one

08:33.586 --> 08:35.321
Who was dissatisfied
with his purchase.

08:35.390 --> 08:37.626
Whoever bought that baby from
you obviously didn't want it.

08:37.694 --> 08:39.964
A baby? I didn't sell a baby.

08:42.637 --> 08:44.072
Look, there's a note.

08:44.140 --> 08:46.979
"glenn, this is your child.

08:47.047 --> 08:48.983
Next time wear
a condom, jerk."

08:49.050 --> 08:50.586
Oh, my god!

08:50.654 --> 08:52.256
Well, now,
hang on, quagmire.

08:52.324 --> 08:54.093
There's no guarantee
it's your baby.

08:54.161 --> 08:55.462
Giggity?

08:55.530 --> 08:57.734
Oh...
I say that.

09:05.275 --> 09:07.011
Well, the dna test
results are back.

09:07.079 --> 09:09.750
This little girl is definitely
your baby, quagmire.

09:10.117 --> 09:11.185
Wh-what am I
supposed to do?

09:11.253 --> 09:12.756
I-I don't want a baby.

09:12.823 --> 09:14.559
Look, somebody's gotta take
this kid off my hands.

09:14.627 --> 09:15.928
I-I can't be a father.

09:15.996 --> 09:17.967
Well, glenn, you don't
have a choice.

09:18.034 --> 09:20.204
This baby is
your responsibility.

09:20.272 --> 09:22.709
Now, I brought you a basket
of things to get you started.

09:22.777 --> 09:25.481
There's baby clothes,
some toys, and some books.

09:25.549 --> 09:27.819
Now, if you have any questions,
we're right across the street.

09:33.465 --> 09:36.403
Hey, what's going on?

09:36.472 --> 09:37.807
(coos)

09:37.874 --> 09:40.946
Not really sure what I'm
supposed to do with you.

09:41.014 --> 09:44.153
There's some frozen steaks
in the freezer.

09:44.220 --> 09:46.658
Bathroom's down the hall
to the right.

09:46.725 --> 09:49.230
Uh, if you ever come home
and there's a tie on the door,

09:49.298 --> 09:50.933
It means I'm froggin' someone,

09:51.000 --> 09:53.571
So give me at least,
uh, a couple hours.

09:53.639 --> 09:55.876
You smoke?

10:00.820 --> 10:02.289
Stewie, what are
you doing here?

10:02.357 --> 10:04.393
I thought you were going to
bobby stalling's birthday party.

10:04.461 --> 10:05.629
Ugh, I hate that kid.

10:05.698 --> 10:07.868
And I hate children's
birthday parties.

10:07.935 --> 10:09.470
I sent bitch stewie
in my place.

10:12.544 --> 10:15.215
Oh, what a great
little party, janet.

10:15.284 --> 10:17.586
You know, I've never seen stewie
come out of his shell so much.

10:19.324 --> 10:21.662
Oh, no, it's not on his tail.

10:21.730 --> 10:24.134
It's on his face.
I've ruined it!

10:24.202 --> 10:26.238
Oh, no, well,
that's okay, though.

10:26.306 --> 10:28.142
Somebody else will come along
and get it right!

10:28.210 --> 10:30.513
Thanks for coming to my
birthday party, stewie.

10:30.581 --> 10:32.651
Oh, I wouldn't have
missed it for anything!

10:32.718 --> 10:34.488
I've never been
to a party before!

10:34.555 --> 10:36.124
Wanna watch me
blow out the candles?

10:36.191 --> 10:37.827
I would love to see that!

10:37.895 --> 10:40.133
And gosh, bobby,
I'd love to play

10:40.200 --> 10:41.602
With some of your
birthday toys,

10:41.670 --> 10:43.038
But only after you've
played with them

10:43.105 --> 10:44.742
And only if you
say it's okay!

10:44.810 --> 10:46.312
You know, stewie,
I gotta say,

10:46.379 --> 10:48.317
That clone of yours
has come in pretty handy.

10:48.384 --> 10:50.453
I, uh, don't suppose
you'd consider

10:50.521 --> 10:52.057
Making one of those
for me, would you?

10:52.125 --> 10:53.927
(chuckles)
maybe.

10:53.995 --> 10:55.764
What would you be
willing to do for me?

10:55.832 --> 10:57.268
What do you want?

10:57.336 --> 10:59.806
Take your index finger
and your thumb

10:59.873 --> 11:01.843
And lightly grip
the base of your tail.

11:01.911 --> 11:03.747
What?

11:03.815 --> 11:05.751
Lightly grip
the base of your tail

11:05.819 --> 11:07.855
With your index finger
and your thumb

11:07.923 --> 11:11.061
And then slide your fingers
up the length of your tail

11:11.129 --> 11:12.264
To the tip.

11:12.332 --> 11:13.467
Why?

11:13.534 --> 11:15.204
Because that's
what I asked you to do.

11:15.271 --> 11:16.473
That's kind of weird.

11:16.540 --> 11:17.843
Is this some kind
of sexual thing?

11:17.910 --> 11:19.479
Nobody said anything
about "sexual."

11:19.547 --> 11:20.915
There's nothing
sexual about it.

11:20.983 --> 11:23.321
I'm just asking you
to perform a simple task.

11:23.389 --> 11:25.992
Take your index finger
and your thumb

11:26.060 --> 11:28.765
And lightly grip
the base of your tail

11:28.832 --> 11:32.204
And run your fingers
along the length of your tail.

11:32.273 --> 11:33.541
You mean, stroke it?

11:33.609 --> 11:35.779
Nobody used that word.
This is not a stroking motion.

11:35.846 --> 11:38.985
This is a completely nonsexual
thing I am asking you to do

11:39.053 --> 11:41.390
In a completely
nonsexual way.

11:41.458 --> 11:43.895
Squeeze the base
of the tail lightly

11:43.962 --> 11:45.999
With your thumb
and index finger

11:46.067 --> 11:48.872
And then,
while continuing to squeeze,

11:48.940 --> 11:52.179
Run them up the length
of your tail to the tip.

11:52.246 --> 11:54.316
And I'll make you a clone.

11:54.384 --> 11:55.953
I only have to do it once?

11:56.021 --> 11:57.890
I'll tell you when to stop.

12:01.732 --> 12:03.034
(laughing):
I don't know
why you're stopping.

12:03.102 --> 12:04.971
Nobody told you to stop.

12:07.411 --> 12:09.914
Give me a little smile.

12:09.982 --> 12:11.317
Your lips look
a little dry.

12:11.384 --> 12:13.187
Why don't you wet 'em
a little bit?

12:14.825 --> 12:15.993
(laughing)

12:16.061 --> 12:18.765
Oh, my god,
you're so weird!

12:18.833 --> 12:20.803
All right, I'll make you
a clone, buddy.

12:23.978 --> 12:26.681
Oh, she's a beautiful
little girl, glenn.

12:26.749 --> 12:28.285
Have you given her
a name yet?

12:28.353 --> 12:29.787
Yeah, I named her
anna lee,

12:29.855 --> 12:31.591
But I'm probably just going
to call her "annal" for short.

12:31.659 --> 12:32.694
That's funny.
Thank you.

12:32.762 --> 12:34.330
Anyway,
thanks for all the baby stuff.

12:34.398 --> 12:35.967
Hey, what's
that big tarp over there?

12:36.035 --> 12:38.372
Oh, that was chris's blankie
from when he was a baby.

12:38.440 --> 12:39.775
Yeah, he was a big kid.

12:39.843 --> 12:41.679
Almost split lois in half,
coming out of her.

12:41.747 --> 12:43.315
It's true.

12:43.383 --> 12:45.387
I never mentioned this because
I don't want him to feel bad,

12:45.454 --> 12:48.660
But after he was born, they had
to rearrange most of my organs.

12:48.727 --> 12:51.132
Oh, yeah. He dragged half
of lois right out with him.

12:51.200 --> 12:53.570
Yeah, the doctors said I'll
be lucky if I live past 50,

12:53.636 --> 12:57.044
But chris is healthy,
and I thank god for that.

12:59.816 --> 13:02.054
Oh, there you are, brian.

13:02.121 --> 13:04.024
All right, you ready
to meet your clone?

13:04.092 --> 13:05.293
Am I ever?

13:05.361 --> 13:07.331
I've got a to-do list
three pages long for him.

13:07.398 --> 13:09.569
Okay, now I want to qualify
this by reminding you

13:09.637 --> 13:11.072
That, as with my clone,

13:11.139 --> 13:12.976
The intelligence level
is reduced a bit.

13:13.043 --> 13:14.612
That's good. We don't
want him thinking too much.

13:14.680 --> 13:16.817
Yeah, well, I might
have dialed yours back

13:16.884 --> 13:17.885
A little more than
I ought to have.

13:17.953 --> 13:19.155
What do you mean?

13:19.223 --> 13:20.858
Brian,
meet bitch brian.

13:20.926 --> 13:24.733
Hi, brian. You got some stuff
you want me to do for you?

13:24.800 --> 13:26.068
Oh, my god.

13:26.137 --> 13:27.872
Yeah. That's kind of
what I said, too.

13:27.940 --> 13:28.974
You know, I'll-I'll be honest
with you, brian.

13:29.042 --> 13:30.177
Here's what happened.

13:30.245 --> 13:31.480
I didn't really want
to do the work,

13:31.547 --> 13:33.484
So bitch stewie
sort of did it.

13:33.551 --> 13:35.822
Hey, stewie,
how'd the clone turn out?

13:35.890 --> 13:38.327
Brian, I can't go
to the bathroom by myself.

13:38.395 --> 13:39.596
Will you please help me?

13:39.664 --> 13:41.300
But I'm good
at other stuff!

13:44.240 --> 13:46.076
(doorbell rings)

13:47.313 --> 13:48.748
Hello, candy.

13:48.815 --> 13:49.950
Hi, glenn.

13:50.018 --> 13:51.888
Come on in.

13:55.128 --> 13:56.898
(retro jazz tune plays)

14:00.673 --> 14:02.409
♪ ♪

14:23.352 --> 14:25.155
So, how long you been
in beauty school?

14:25.223 --> 14:26.457
Two months.

14:26.525 --> 14:27.827
Well, tonight we're
doing facials.

14:29.766 --> 14:30.867
(baby crying)

14:30.934 --> 14:33.806
Oh, god. Hang on a second.

14:35.443 --> 14:37.580
Okay, okay. Stop.
Just stop crying.

14:37.648 --> 14:39.183
Stop crying, anna lee.

14:39.251 --> 14:41.087
Oh, no wonder. You
dropped your pacifier.

14:42.458 --> 14:45.096
(buzzes)

14:48.002 --> 14:49.471
You have a baby?

14:49.539 --> 14:50.774
Yeah. It's a long story.

14:50.842 --> 14:52.812
Damn kid's kept me up
every night for two weeks.

14:52.879 --> 14:54.381
Now, where were we?

14:54.449 --> 14:55.716
Giggity-giggity...

14:55.784 --> 14:58.222
(snoring)

15:06.539 --> 15:08.977
<i>Candy:
Glenn, you fell asleep,
so I took off.</i>

15:09.045 --> 15:10.681
<i>It's probably for the best.</i>

15:10.748 --> 15:12.350
<i>I've never had sex before,</i>

15:12.419 --> 15:14.254
<i>And I probably wouldn't
have been much good at it.</i>

15:14.323 --> 15:15.891
(screaming)

15:15.959 --> 15:17.193
(anna lee crying)

15:17.261 --> 15:19.398
That's it.
That kid is out of here.

15:19.466 --> 15:21.569
Hey, there's another note.

15:21.637 --> 15:25.042
"glenn, this is your child.
Next time wear a condom, jer..."

15:25.111 --> 15:27.682
Oh, that's the note
from earlier.

15:27.750 --> 15:28.951
I...

15:29.019 --> 15:30.287
Need a file cabinet.

15:35.347 --> 15:38.051
So, it's just not working out,
me being a father.

15:38.118 --> 15:39.353
And that's why I'm wondering

15:39.421 --> 15:41.390
If you and lois would be
willing to adopt the baby.

15:41.458 --> 15:43.294
Uh... Oh, boy, quagmire.

15:43.362 --> 15:44.697
I-I don't know
that we can do that.

15:44.764 --> 15:46.667
We-we-we can barely take
care of the two we have.

15:46.736 --> 15:48.571
Now-now, this is
just a suggestion.

15:48.640 --> 15:51.478
Just throwing it out there.
Have you considered abortion?

15:51.546 --> 15:53.549
Uh, peter, I think
it's too late for that.

15:53.617 --> 15:55.621
Oh, don't let the press
put the scare into you.

15:55.687 --> 15:57.724
Wade v. Boggs has
not been overturned.

15:57.791 --> 16:00.196
Yeah, but you can't really
abort a live baby.

16:00.263 --> 16:02.367
Ho, boy, they have got you.

16:02.434 --> 16:04.204
Glenn, glenn.

16:04.271 --> 16:06.074
(whispering):
Give her back to god.

16:06.142 --> 16:08.212
Peter, I'm going to go ahead and
move the conversation forward.

16:08.279 --> 16:10.182
Is there any way
you guys could take anna lee?

16:10.250 --> 16:11.351
No, quagmire.

16:11.419 --> 16:12.654
We got enough kids of our own,

16:12.721 --> 16:13.823
Plus ol' brian over there.

16:13.891 --> 16:15.092
Right, buddy?

16:15.160 --> 16:16.863
I sharpened a
pencil in my bum

16:16.930 --> 16:18.633
And now I need
a band-aid.

16:23.944 --> 16:26.182
You're doing
the right thing, quagmire.

16:26.250 --> 16:28.219
All right, quagmire, just so
you're clear on the law,

16:28.287 --> 16:30.624
Once you give this child up
to the adoption agency,

16:30.692 --> 16:33.263
You can no longer abort it.

16:33.330 --> 16:34.865
Hello, sir.

16:34.933 --> 16:36.703
Do you wish to put this
child up for adoption?

16:36.770 --> 16:37.872
Yeah.
It's not working out.

16:37.940 --> 16:39.108
I need to get her
out of my hair.

16:39.176 --> 16:40.310
Well, we can
help you there.

16:40.378 --> 16:41.813
Is it a boy or a girl?

16:41.880 --> 16:43.850
It's a girl.
Her name's anna lee.

16:43.918 --> 16:45.120
Oh, beautiful name.

16:45.188 --> 16:46.255
Let me take her from you.

16:50.432 --> 16:52.635
Well, go on, quagmire.
Give her the baby.

16:52.702 --> 16:54.172
I-I will.

16:54.240 --> 16:55.407
I-I just...

16:58.048 --> 16:59.649
Oh...

16:59.717 --> 17:01.119
Here.

17:01.187 --> 17:04.359
She, uh... She'll go
to a good home, right?

17:04.427 --> 17:05.795
Oh, yes.

17:05.863 --> 17:07.298
She'll be
somewhere safe, right?

17:07.366 --> 17:09.703
Like, you're not going to put
her with sand people, right?

17:09.771 --> 17:11.640
<i>You mean like
from star wars?</i>

17:11.708 --> 17:13.912
(laughs)
no, no, no, no, no.

17:16.851 --> 17:19.957
Brian, I didn't know if
you wanted a god's eye,

17:20.025 --> 17:21.093
But I made you one.

17:21.161 --> 17:22.328
Uh...

17:22.396 --> 17:23.931
Okay, thank you.

17:23.999 --> 17:25.669
Did you wash my car,
like I asked?

17:25.737 --> 17:27.373
No, but I hit it
with a rock.

17:27.440 --> 17:29.009
Okay, thanks.

17:29.076 --> 17:31.680
Brian, I think my jaw
is falling off.

17:31.749 --> 17:33.417
Oh! Oh, g...

17:33.485 --> 17:34.888
Stewie, what is happening
to this thing?!

17:34.955 --> 17:37.626
Oh, yeah. Turns out the clones
aren't too stable, brian.

17:37.694 --> 17:39.564
I've been having
some trouble with mine, too.

17:39.631 --> 17:42.770
Hey, stewie, everything sounds
like rushing water.

17:42.838 --> 17:45.142
And I can't stand up
so very good.

17:45.210 --> 17:46.878
Yeah, I figure they've got
less than a minute

17:46.946 --> 17:48.381
Before they
dissolve completely.

17:48.449 --> 17:50.385
Hey, brian?
Knock-knock.

17:50.453 --> 17:51.588
Who's there?

17:51.655 --> 17:52.924
(passes gas)

17:52.992 --> 17:54.995
(laughing)

17:57.032 --> 17:59.503
Whoa. I hope
that doesn't happen to me.

18:01.342 --> 18:02.776
He took my dry cleaning

18:02.844 --> 18:04.915
And I have no idea
what he did with the ticket.

18:04.983 --> 18:07.152
Yeah, this was not
a fruitful endeavor.

18:07.220 --> 18:10.192
I'm not proud of this,
but I need to lick that up.

18:13.400 --> 18:15.236
(hard rock playing)

18:16.506 --> 18:17.741
This will be great,
quagmire.

18:17.808 --> 18:20.079
A nudie bar is
the perfect way to celebrate

18:20.147 --> 18:21.382
Your first night
without a baby.

18:21.449 --> 18:22.584
Yeah, peter,
this is great.

18:22.653 --> 18:23.987
I feel like myself again.

18:24.055 --> 18:26.492
I'll tell ya, my life was
so dominated by that baby.

18:26.559 --> 18:27.828
I'm glad she's gone.

18:27.896 --> 18:28.997
Eh, you know sometimes,
you just got

18:29.065 --> 18:30.667
To make a decision
and go with it.

18:30.734 --> 18:32.972
Like when I decided to try
that radical penis enlargement.

18:34.642 --> 18:35.944
Peter, I don't think...

18:36.012 --> 18:37.415
Brian, your objections
are duly noted.

18:37.481 --> 18:38.684
Now hit the gas!

18:38.751 --> 18:39.819
(tires squealing)

18:40.956 --> 18:42.290
(loud snapping)

18:42.359 --> 18:45.296
You know that would never work
again in a million years.

18:45.364 --> 18:46.833
Don't need it to, brian.

18:49.873 --> 18:52.178
Heh. That stripper
has a rash on her ass,

18:52.244 --> 18:53.613
Just like anna lee
used to get.

18:53.681 --> 18:55.351
Uh, yeah.

18:55.418 --> 18:57.288
And that other stripper's
sitting on that guy's lap,

18:57.356 --> 18:58.958
Just like anna lee used to do.

18:59.026 --> 19:00.561
I guess.

19:00.628 --> 19:03.333
And that stripper only has
one tooth, just like anna lee.

19:03.401 --> 19:04.937
Quagmire,
you feeling okay?

19:05.005 --> 19:06.272
I don't know.

19:06.340 --> 19:08.110
I think I might have
made a terrible mistake.

19:08.177 --> 19:10.180
I abandoned my daughter!

19:10.248 --> 19:12.685
Why did I give away
my only daughter?!

19:12.753 --> 19:14.455
(sobbing):
Oh...

19:14.523 --> 19:16.526
Oh, god.

19:16.594 --> 19:18.397
(sobbing)

19:18.464 --> 19:19.900
He'll be fine.

19:19.968 --> 19:21.337
We shouldn't let this
ruin our night.

19:21.405 --> 19:23.107
Let's just enjoy
the strippers.

19:23.175 --> 19:24.476
I guess.

19:24.544 --> 19:26.647
I just hate the way that one
gets so into her work.

19:26.715 --> 19:28.819
You boys have
been very naughty.

19:28.887 --> 19:31.992
I'm going to have to
assign you extra homework.

19:32.060 --> 19:34.930
Darn it.
Fractions are so hard.

19:34.998 --> 19:36.600
What did you get
for number four?

19:36.668 --> 19:38.371
She said, "don't
share answers"!

19:41.646 --> 19:43.848
All right, here
it is: 625 maple.

19:43.916 --> 19:45.585
That's the family
that adopted anna lee.

19:47.824 --> 19:49.593
Hey, wait, wait.
Guys?!

19:49.661 --> 19:53.969
Well, it's just me
and my old nemesis, first step.

19:54.037 --> 19:55.138
(laughing)

19:55.206 --> 19:56.341
Hey, joe, what you doing?

19:56.409 --> 19:57.577
You out for a walk?

19:57.644 --> 19:59.246
I hate this block.

20:01.752 --> 20:02.887
(gasps)
there she is!

20:02.955 --> 20:03.956
There's anna lee!

20:06.929 --> 20:08.332
Hang on, anna lee.
I'm coming.

20:08.399 --> 20:09.400
(grunting)

20:11.205 --> 20:12.473
(gasps)
it's them.

20:19.990 --> 20:22.126
Look at her.

20:22.194 --> 20:24.364
She looks so happy.

20:24.431 --> 20:27.471
Almost like she belongs there.

20:27.539 --> 20:30.176
They look like a real family.

20:30.243 --> 20:33.015
I can't take her
away from this.

20:33.083 --> 20:34.685
Joe:
What's happening?!

20:34.753 --> 20:36.255
He's not going
to go through with it!

20:36.323 --> 20:38.827
It's a nice family and the kid
will be better off here!

20:38.894 --> 20:40.430
Aw, that's sweet!

20:40.498 --> 20:42.768
What's the inside
of the house look like?!

20:42.835 --> 20:44.271
Colonial!
Furniture's pretty good!

20:44.339 --> 20:46.042
Possibly imported area rug!

20:46.109 --> 20:47.411
Oh, that's nice!

20:47.478 --> 20:49.583
A bit pricey, but for
the money you're spending,

20:49.650 --> 20:51.352
You know, it's not
a bad way to go!

20:51.420 --> 20:52.521
Yeah, for the money!

20:52.589 --> 20:53.723
You ready to go, quagmire?

20:53.791 --> 20:55.193
Yeah.

20:55.261 --> 20:57.631
You know, I got to tell you,
I think you did a good thing.

20:57.699 --> 21:00.504
Well, I guess I just realized
it's not about me.

21:00.572 --> 21:03.009
This family is what's
best for anna lee.

21:03.077 --> 21:04.913
This is her home now.

21:04.981 --> 21:06.616
I got to let her go.

21:06.683 --> 21:07.952
I'm proud of you, quagmire.

21:08.021 --> 21:09.723
Thanks, man.
Hey, who knows?

21:09.790 --> 21:11.192
Maybe I'll bump
into her in 18 years.

21:11.261 --> 21:12.662
What?!

21:12.730 --> 21:14.633
Did you really think I was
going to change that much?

21:14.700 --> 21:16.035
Good night, everybody!

21:16.036 --> 22:17.036
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru